    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Solve $25^{-x}=125$.",
    "solution_text": "Rewrite both sides with base $5$, retaining the negative index.\n$\\begin{align*}(5^{2})^{-x}&=5^{3}\\\\5^{-2x}&=5^{3}\\\\-2x&=3\\\\x&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Solve $7^{3n-12}=1$.",
    "solution_text": "Write $1$ as $7^{0}$.\n$\\begin{align*}7^{3n-12}&=7^{0}\\\\3n-12&=0\\\\3n&=12\\\\n&=4\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Solve $4^{x+2}=8^{2x-1}$.",
    "solution_text": "Rewrite both sides with base $2$. Multiply through every term in each bracketed index.\n$\\begin{align*}2^{2(x+2)}&=2^{3(2x-1)}\\\\2^{2x+4}&=2^{6x-3}\\\\2x+4&=6x-3\\\\7&=4x\\\\x&=\\frac{7}{4}\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Solve $\\left(\\frac{3}{7}\\right)^{2x+1}=\\frac{49}{9}$.",
    "solution_text": "Express the right-hand side as a power of the same fractional base.\n$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{3}{7}\\right)^{2x+1}&=\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left(\\frac{3}{7}\\right)^{2x+1}&=\\left(\\frac{3}{7}\\right)^{-2}\\\\2x+1&=-2\\\\2x&=-3\\\\x&=-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Solve $49^{x}=\\sqrt[3]{343}$.",
    "solution_text": "Convert the root to a fractional index and use base $7$.\n$\\begin{align*}7^{2x}&=(7^{3})^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\\\7^{2x}&=7^{1}\\\\2x&=1\\\\x&=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Solve $2^{x}=0.0625$.",
    "solution_text": "Rewrite the decimal as a fraction first.\n$\\begin{align*}2^{x}&=\\frac{1}{16}\\\\2^{x}&=2^{-4}\\\\x&=-4\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Solve $3^{5x}\\times9^{-2x+1}=81$.",
    "solution_text": "Use base $3$, then add the indices of the multiplied powers.\n$\\begin{align*}3^{5x}\\times3^{2(-2x+1)}&=3^{4}\\\\3^{5x}\\times3^{-4x+2}&=3^{4}\\\\3^{x+2}&=3^{4}\\\\x+2&=4\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Solve $\\frac{25^{n+2}}{5^{n}}=125$.",
    "solution_text": "Use base $5$, then subtract the denominator's index from the numerator's index.\n$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5^{2n+4}}{5^{n}}&=5^{3}\\\\5^{(2n+4)-n}&=5^{3}\\\\5^{n+4}&=5^{3}\\\\n+4&=3\\\\n&=-1\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  }
]
